#71101
"Walkway Around the Pyramid"
"From here, you can see several layers of ramps leading up to the very top of

the pyramid.  Set within the upward ramp is a smaller ramp that slopes down

into the bowels of the massive edifice.  The steeply inclined walls and the

less angled ramps all lend to an odd visual effect that makes it impossible to

estimate the height of the pyramid.  The structure appears to only have two

floors above the base level on which you stand.  The walkway stone here

appears to be carved with the image of a reptilian creature of unknown species.

"
"Lizard

