#71103
"Walkway Around the Pyramid"
"Between the encroaching jungle to the north and east and the imposing stone

walls of the pyramid's corner, this area possesses a somewhat claustrophobic

air despite how relatively open it actually is.  Roughly equally far to the

west and south lie dark openings that presumably lead deeper into the pyramid

here.  Unlike to the west, the southern opening appears to be set within a

large ramp leading upwards to a higher level of the pyramid.  The walkway

stone here appears to have been carved with greater detail than many of the

other stones surrounding the structure.

"
"Sst'rasa

