#71111
"Walkway Around the Pyramid"
"Set in the pyramid wall to the north, a dark ramp leads downward into the

heart of the pyramid.  The stone walkway here is divided between two massive

stones that meet at the midpoint of the tunnel leading below.  Both stones

seem curiously empty of design, or even debris, but the western stone feels

almost tangibly colder, as though the lurking shadows from overhanging jungle

foliage refuse to allow light onto its surface.  The east stone, by contrast

seems clear and open, the only shadows that seem to drift across it are from

the distant clouds overhead.

"
"Xiroce + Sky

