#71113
"Walkway Around the Pyramid"
"The perfectly even angles and distances between the far eastern and northern

corners of the pyramid suggest a fairly advanced culture built this structure,

but it does not appear to resemble the work of any of the major races of the

realm.  A large, carved circle is in the middle of the walkway stone here with

several carved lines running through it.  Tall jungle plants line the edge of

the stone, but none seem inclined to lean over this section of the walkway.

Consequently, almost no leaves or other debris distract from the pattern here.

"
